{"id":"b92e2f4704824ad8f28509bda363989add0818c7","axis":"silent","repo":"oven-sh/bun","sha":"b92e2f4704824ad8f28509bda363989add0818c7","parsed":{"files":[{"path":"docs/runtime/check.mdx","lines":["@@ -654,6 +654,7 @@ These differences are intentional:"," - **There is no `bun check --watch`.** To check again on every change, use [`bun --watch --check`](#watch-mode)."," - **The order of files does not change the errors.** `tsc` collects the errors of a file right after it checks that file, so it drops an error that a later file raises in an earlier one. `bun check` reports it."," - **A file that is too long affects no other file.** After TS2563 for the top-level code of one file, `tsc` stops following the types of variables and parameters in the files it checks next, so it drops errors there and reports false ones. `bun check` starts every file afresh.","+- **The order of projects does not change their options.** If configuration files extend each other in a circle, both tools report TS18000. `tsc` prints `{0}` where the files belong, and `bun check` lists them. What `tsc -b` then makes of those files for one project depends on which project it loaded first, and it can hang. `bun check -b` gives each project the options it has when you check it alone."," - **The `lib.*.d.ts` files are built in.** An error or a declaration in one of them has a path such as `bundled:///libs/lib.dom.d.ts`, which is not a file on your disk."," - **A note tells you when dependencies are missing.** If an import fails because a package in `package.json` is not installed, `bun check` adds a line that names the `package.json` and says how to run `bun install` for it."," - **A note tells you when type checking did not run.** If a syntax error or an invalid option stops the check, `bun check` adds a line that says [how many files it did not check](#stopped-before-type-checking)."],"additions":1,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"src/sema/check/errors_access.rs","lines":["@@ -1293,9 +1293,